            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "h0nqTK",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1060,
              "content": "The compact app bar carries the brand, the account and sign out, and no navigation. That was right while Overview was the only destination and is a gap now there are two. Candidates: a bottom tab bar, a segmented control under the page header, or a nav trigger opening a sheet. A bottom tab bar is the smallest thing that works for two destinations and the easiest to outgrow. Not drawn, because picking it here would make the canvas the decision. If it is wrong, the compact screens gain a bar and lose 56 px of list.",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-sm",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
