              "id": "IPlbn",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "OPEN DECISION · a ledger longer than a screen",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "bXCjy",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1060,
              "content": "Nothing here pages or loads more. The specs do not ask for it and the library has a Pagination molecule that would fit, so drawing one would answer a question nobody asked. A household reaching ninety days at five accounts will want something. If it is wrong, the ledger gains a footer.",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-sm",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "h2CNx",
          "name": "NOTE · the row is not the library's row",
          "width": 1100,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "fjxXn",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "NOTE · the row is not the library's row",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "jZYBX",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1060,
              "content": "The library's Transaction row carries a category column, which this change does not have, and no account and no settled marker, which it needs. The rows here are drawn in this file. See canvas.md, Components missing.",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-sm",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "rLoYu",
          "name": "NOTE · Monzo is the interpolated bank",
          "width": 1100,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "aEjbn",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "NOTE · Monzo is the interpolated bank",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "l4XW9",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1060,
              "content": "Copy that names a bank uses Monzo, matching 02-banking, so the canvas contract reads it as a template rather than as fixture text. Montepio is the household's second bank and appears only in data.",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-sm",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "ii9SB",
          "name": "NOTE · the shell disables what does not exist",
          "width": 1100,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "QcYvB",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "NOTE · the shell disables what does not exist",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "thR9n",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1060,
              "content": "Signed-in landing switches off every destination but Overview. Each screen here turns Transactions back on and moves the current marker onto it. Adding a destination is a change to that template's overrides, not a new component.",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-sm",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "nAfJV",
          "name": "Finding a month is not its own journey",
          "width": 1240,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "pibFb",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "Finding a month is not its own journey",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-heading-sm",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "v7iOs",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "A journey is a user goal. Finding what happened in April is the same goal as seeing where the money went, reached by a different move, so the month strip is drawn into J07 rather than given a J number of its own. It appears on every Transactions frame in this file, because it is part of the screen and not a mode of it.\n\nJumping to a month is drawn as 05, with its own fixture: the strip says April and so do the rows, the day headings and the span. A frame whose control claims one month while its rows show another teaches the control wrong.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "j4Yqx",
          "name": "The waiting state belongs to every screen, and is drawn once",
          "width": 1240,
          "fill": "$ui:color-bg-surface",
          "cornerRadius": "$ui:radius-md",
          "stroke": "$ui:color-border-default",
          "strokeWidth": 1,
          "strokeAlignment": "inner",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 8,
          "padding": 20,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "D8AnIp",
              "name": "Title",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-primary",
              "content": "The waiting state belongs to every screen, and is drawn once",
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-heading-sm",
              "fontWeight": "600"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vpxX3",
              "name": "Note",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "00 · Waiting for the screen is drawn on Transactions because that is the screen with the slowest arrival, and it is the only place it is drawn. The bar is one component in the root shell, identical on every screen, and drawing it eight times would say it was eight decisions.\n\nThe drawing is the visible half. The half that cannot be drawn is the announcement, the 150 ms before it appears and the 400 ms it stays once it has. All three are contracts in the change's canvas record and are verified in code.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
              "fontSize": "$ui:type-size-body-md",
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
